            "text": "The most common employment arrangement in the United States is W-2 employment. If you work for a company and receive a regular paycheck on a set schedule, you are almost certainly a W-2 employee. The name comes from the IRS Form W-2, which your employer issues at the end of each year summarizing your total earnings and tax withholdings."
